<title>FRANCE: LVMH, Dior up sharply.</title>
<headline>LVMH, Dior up sharply.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in LVMH and Dior rose sharply after the luxury group announced a 68 percent rise in its first quarter sales.</p>
<p>At 1023 GMT, LVMH was up 4.58 percent at 1,346 francs while Christian Dior was 3.57 higher percent at 842 francs.</p>
<p>&quot;The sales figures were excellent,&quot; a trader said.</p>
<p>Christian Dior has a 41.7 percent stake in LVMH.</p>
<p>The LVMH sales were up 10.4 percent on a like-for-like basis as LVMH consolidated DFS Group Ltd and Celine for the first time.</p>
</text>
